# ARag APP-TIER per-deploy image tags — the compose env-file that rides in the S3
# deploy bundle (NOT user-data), so an image bump never reprovisions the host.
#
# App tier only: the two images the ui+api+mcp compose stack runs. The arag-ingest
# image is deployed separately by the on-demand ingest runner (A7), not from here.
#
# scripts/deploy_arag_bundle.py substitutes ${REGISTRY} (the in-account ECR host,
# derived from STS at upload time — which is why the real account id is not
# committed here) and uploads the result to s3://<filings>/deploy/deploy.env.
# app-deploy.sh passes it as compose's SECOND --env-file, so these win over the
# image placeholders in docker-compose.aws.yml.
#
# TO BUMP AN IMAGE: edit a tag below (or pass --tag to the script to fill
# arm64-SETME), re-run scripts/deploy_arag_bundle.py, then `systemctl restart
# app.service` on the host (SSM). No Terraform, no reprovision. Tags are immutable
# (never :latest); a tag is a reliable record of what runs.
ARAG_IMAGE=${REGISTRY}/genai-dev/arag:arm64-SETME
ARAG_UI_IMAGE=${REGISTRY}/genai-dev/arag-ui:arm64-SETME
